# branding/manifest — files this fork substitutes wholesale into the checkout.
#
# `./scripts/redrob.py brand` copies each SOURCE over its TARGET in chromium/src.
# KIND decides what happens at `export` time, and the distinction is the point:
#
# `./scripts/redrob.py brand` copies each SOURCE over its TARGET in chromium/src.
# Every row here is applied by `brand` and excluded from `export`: the file in this
# directory IS the review surface, and also emitting a patch for it would give the
# same content two sources of truth. KIND records what kind of file it is, which is
# what tells a reader whether the diff below is readable at all:
#
#   text    a small configuration file we own in full. Reviewable here.
#   binary  an icon. Reviewable only by looking at it; branding/make-icons.sh is how
#           it was produced, and that script is the thing to review instead.
#
# The bump sequence is therefore sync -> brand -> apply -> export: `brand` lays down
# these files, `apply` puts the hand-written patches on top.
#
# Files Chromium does not have at all are neither branding nor patches; they live under
# sources/ and are declared in sources/manifest, which `redrob.py apply` copies in.
#
# Format: SOURCE  TARGET  KIND


