# The scaled sets. theme_resources.grd resolves IDR_PRODUCT_LOGO_16 / _32 out of
# default_{100,200}_percent, so the window and tab icon come from here rather than from the
# unscaled directory above -- replacing only the latter leaves a Chromium icon in the tab strip.
branding/icons/product_logo_16.png      chrome/app/theme/default_100_percent/chromium/product_logo_16.png       binary
branding/icons/product_logo_32.png      chrome/app/theme/default_100_percent/chromium/product_logo_32.png       binary
branding/icons/product_logo_16.png      chrome/app/theme/default_100_percent/chromium/linux/product_logo_16.png binary
# The 32px LINUX icon, which was missing and shipped Chromium's blue globe in the .deb.
#
# Line 47 covers default_100_percent/chromium/product_logo_32.png and line 41 covers linux/product_logo_32.xpm,
# so the set LOOKED complete from either direction -- there was a 32 and there was a linux/32. The one the
# installer actually copies is default_100_percent/chromium/linux/product_logo_32.png, a fourth path, and at
# standard DPI it is the icon a Linux desktop shows in the launcher and the window title.
branding/icons/product_logo_32.png      chrome/app/theme/default_100_percent/chromium/linux/product_logo_32.png binary
